== v1.6-011 ==
* Error reports
  * An unexpected error no longer ends the program. A window shows the error report (CutiePie version, time, library versions and the traceback) with a "Copy to clipboard" button, to paste into a bug report.
  * This covers errors in buttons and menus, timers, background threads, and while the main window starts up.
  * Errors in mouse and key actions on the plots, which used to do nothing and print only to the terminal, show the same window.
  * The same error repeating is counted on one report instead of opening more windows.
* Plot CSV (Extra tab)
  * A file that cannot be read shows a popup with the error message instead of ending the program.
== v1.6-011 ==

== v1.6-010 ==
* Fits (Extra tab)
  * New "Clear fit" button under the Fit button removes all fit drawings (lines, peak labels, legend) from the selected spectrum.
* Plot CSV (Extra tab)
  * New "CSV from" choice above the Plot CSV button: SpecTcl (plain x,y rows, as before) or InterSpec.
  * InterSpec files (header lines followed by a Channel,Energy,Counts table) are plotted as counts against energy and can be fitted with Fit CSV.
== v1.6-010 ==

== v1.6-009 ==
* Fits (Extra tab)
  * The fit drawings (total and component lines, peak labels, legend) follow the spectrum into the enlarged view and back; they used to disappear on enlarging and were lost after shrinking.
  * A fit made in the enlarged view stays on the spectrum after leaving it.
  * The fit legend is clipped at the edges of its spectrum instead of running over the neighbouring ones.
  * Fit drawings no longer shrink the spectra when the window is resized or the view is refreshed.
  * A turning ring on the Fit button shows that a fit is running.
* Mouse wheel on the spectrum under the cursor
  * Wheel zooms the x axis in (wheel up) or out (wheel down) around the cursor position.
  * Zooming a 1D spectrum in or out also sets the top of the y axis to fit the highest bin in view.
  * Shift+wheel moves the x axis of a zoomed-in spectrum by one fifth of the visible range (this was the plain wheel in v1.6-008).
  * Ctrl+wheel changes the y scale like the + and - buttons (wheel up is +).
* Peak Finder
  * Clicking the empty area of the fitted-peaks table cancels the row selection and puts the "Peaks" menu back on Auto.
  * A new peak always starts on Auto, and making one puts the "Peaks" menu back on Auto.
  * A new peak is selected in the fitted-peaks table.
  * Changing the "Peaks" menu to Auto on a selected fit refits it with the automatic number of Gaussians.
* Closing the main window closes all other CutiePie windows, so the program exits.
== v1.6-009 ==

== v1.6-008 ==
* Gates
  * Gates can be created in any view; the spectrum no longer has to be enlarged first.
  * With no spectrum selected, pressing Gate and then clicking a spectrum starts the gate on it.
  * After leaving the enlarged view, gates are drawn on every spectrum and the plots are refreshed as the Update button does.
  * The default gate name is numbered over all SpecTcl gates, not only those of the selected spectrum.
  * In gate edit mode, changing the selected gate restores the previous gate's color.
  * Gates stay visible when entering the enlarged view with autoscale off (they used to appear only after Update).
* Peak Finder
  * Fitted peaks are also drawn in the enlarged view.
  * The label under the fitted-peaks table lists every Gaussian of a fit.
  * New "Peaks" menu (Auto, 1-5) sets the number of Gaussians in a fit by hand.
* The mouse wheel moves the x axis of a zoomed-in spectrum under the cursor by one fifth of the visible range per scroll (wheel down toward higher x).
